<div class="wprm-recipe-summary wprm-block-text-normal"><span style="display: block;">Sweet Potatoes are not common in the Mediterranean, but that doesn&rsquo;t mean we cannot use them in a salad that embodies the flavors of the region. Made by roasting sweet potatoes tossed with chickpeas, feta, and candied walnuts and serving them on a bed of arugula, this make-ahead salad is worthy of your holiday table as a colorful centerpiece or a humble yet filling lunch to take to work with you on a Tuesday.</span></div>
